From: yt6801-builder <builder@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: port dwmac-motorcomm glue to kernel 6.6 PCI iomap API

pcim_iomap_region() only exists from v6.9 onwards. Kernel 6.6.144 (the
kernel used by iStoreOS 24.10) still uses the two-step API
pcim_iomap_regions() + pcim_iomap_table(), exactly like the in-tree
stmmac_pci.c and dwmac-intel.c glues.

Rewrite the BAR mapping in motorcomm_probe() accordingly so the YT6801
glue driver builds on 6.6.

---


--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-motorcomm.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-motorcomm.c
@@ -299,10 +299,17 @@
 		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, ret,
 				     "failed to enable device\n");
 
-	priv->base = pcim_iomap_region(pdev, 0, DRIVER_NAME);
-	if (IS_ERR(priv->base))
-		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, PTR_ERR(priv->base),
-				     "failed to map IO region\n");
+	/*
+	 * Kernel 6.6 lacks pcim_iomap_region(); use the older two-step API
+	 * that the in-tree stmmac PCI glues (stmmac_pci.c / dwmac-intel.c)
+	 * still rely on for this kernel generation.
+	 */
+	ret = pcim_iomap_regions(pdev, BIT(0), DRIVER_NAME);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, ret,
+				     "failed to request/map IO region\n");
+
+	priv->base = pcim_iomap_table(pdev)[0];
 
 	pci_set_master(pdev);
 
